nodecode-off-peak is a rewrite of onkanat's onkanat/hermes-offpeak-bekci:

  https://github.com/onkanat/hermes-offpeak-bekci
  commit e566f9101be4bc9e8084e8f09b27bb7fbd551a04
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Hakan Kılıçaslan (onkanat) (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the window arithmetic (peak is Monday to Friday 12:00-18:00 UTC,
and all day at the weekend is off-peak), the countdown and the window's next
change, the markdown ledger of queued work in both shapes the original read (a
table row, or a bullet with `id:` and `status:` fields), the counts by status,
the user-only approval that rewrites one item's status and nothing else, the
JSON status line, the suggested cron job printed in full with the hash of its
plan, and the one-shot notice before the window opens. All of it is Common
Lisp in cell.lisp against Nodecode's cell contract, with no part of the
original's Python or JavaScript carried over.

Left out: the Hermes desktop status-bar chip and its title-bar badge; the
`llm_execution` middleware, which measured the call rate of Ollama Cloud
calls inside the peak window and could, once configured, sleep them -- a
per-call seam Nodecode's cells do not have; the `on_session_end` hook's JSONL
measurement log, replaced by the reminder's standing notice; and the two
install/removal commands that injected a cron request into a Hermes session,
replaced by `/off-peak plan`, which prints the job for the shipped cron cell
to install.
